# CSV files are stored LF in the repo, always.
#
# The matching tools write these with Python's csv module, whose writer emits
# CRLF line terminators (RFC 4180) regardless of platform. Left alone, one
# machine commits a CRLF copy and another an LF copy of the same generated
# table (filing.csv, report.csv, the config maps), and git -- unable to align a
# single line -- reports the WHOLE file as conflicting on every merge between
# them. Normalising to LF in the index makes those diffs line up again, so a
# concurrent-session merge touches only the rows that actually changed.
*.csv text eol=lf
